  "description": "A ceramic triple duct flute of the Tenenexpan type. Separate air ducts feed three tubular resonators together; unequal bore lengths and finger-hole distributions permit simultaneous contrasting pitches. Experimental replicas support present-day investigation and improvisation without recovering a lost ancient repertoire.",
